WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.522
Structured techniques are most valuable when used consistently.

2
00:00:03.522 --> 00:00:13.460
Analysts should remain curious, document assumptions, welcome feedback, communicate uncertainty honestly, and revise conclusions when evidence changes.

3
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.845
Analytical discipline requires humility.

4
00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:22.490
A strong analyst can explain confidence levels, acknowledge gaps, and separate what is known from what is inferred.

5
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:27.050
Over time, these habits improve both individual and team performance.

6
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.809
They make analysis easier to review, challenge, brief, and update.

7
00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:33.476
The goal is not perfection.

8
00:00:33.476 --> 00:00:39.802
The goal is becoming more thoughtful, transparent, and disciplined in how judgments are formed and communicated.
